
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

//Estado del servicio
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1.1 Registrar usuario  (201)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carlos Zatarain",
  "email": "carlos@example.com",
  "password": "secreto123"
}

### 1.2 Registrar con correo repetido (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carlos Zatarain",
  "email": "carlos@example.com",
  "password": "secreto123"
}

### 1.3 Login  (200)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carlos@example.com",
  "password": "secreto123"
}

### 1.4 Login con contraseña incorrecta (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carlos@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1.5 Perfil con token (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.6 Perfil sin token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me

### 1.7 Login como admin (200)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@tienda.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

###
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 2.1 Crear producto (201)  copia el _id de la respuesta
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hoodie ",
  "description": "Hoodie azul marino",
  "price": 899,
  "stock": 5,
  "size": ["M", "L"]
}

### 2.2 Crear producto sin token (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gorra", "price": 250, "stock": 10, "size": "U" }

### 2.3 Listar productos (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

###
@productId = {{createProduct.response.body._id}}

### 2.4 Detalle de producto (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}

### 2.5 Producto inexistente (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/000000000000000000000000

### 3.1 Crear pedido (201)  el total lo calcula el servidor
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [ { "_id": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 2 } ]
}

### 3.2 Pedido con cantidad mayor al stock (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [ { "_id": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 999 } ]
}

### 3.3 Mis pedidos (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/my-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Entregable 2 ----------

### 4.1 Cliente intenta crear un producto (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gorra", "price": 250, "stock": 10, "size": "U" }

### 4.2 Admin edita el producto (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 799, "stock": 8 }

### 4.3 Editar con stock negativo (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": -5 }

### 4.4 Cliente intenta borrar el producto (403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.5 Admin ve todos los usuarios (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4.6 Cliente intenta ver los usuarios (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.7 Admin cambia el rol del cliente a admin (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{login.response.body.user.id}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### 4.8 Admin intenta cambiar su propio rol (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminLogin.response.body.user.id}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "customer" }

### 4.9 Admin ve todos los pedidos con el cliente que los hizo (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5.1 Buscar por nombre (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=hoodie

### 5.2 Filtrar por talla, precio y existencias, ordenado por precio (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?size=M&minPrice=300&maxPrice=1000&inStock=true&sort=price_asc

### 5.3 Precio mínimo mayor al máximo (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?minPrice=900&maxPrice=100

### 6.1 Admin borra el producto (200) - va al final porque las pruebas de arriba usan este producto
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
